# Paperclip Cloudflare edge — Alchemy stack configuration.
# Copy to deploy/cloudflare/.env (gitignored). CI writes its own copy; see README.md.
#
# Cloudflare credentials are NOT set here. Run `pnpm alchemy profile edit --add Cloudflare`
# once (OAuth; choose "Custom Scopes" and pick the scopes listed in
# README.md) or export CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN / CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID.
#
# Login is Paperclip's own account system; nothing here configures who may sign in.

# ---------- Required ----------

# Public hostname for the board. Its zone must be in this Cloudflare account.
PAPERCLIP_HOSTNAME=paperclip.example.com

# ---------- Optional ----------

# Cloudflare zone (name or 32-char id). Inferred from PAPERCLIP_HOSTNAME when unset.
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE=example.com

# R2 bucket for uploads (Paperclip S3 storage). PAPERCLIP_R2_ASSETS=true creates
# paperclip-assets-<stage>; PAPERCLIP_R2_BUCKET names the bucket instead and turns R2 on by
# itself. A bucket that already exists under that name is adopted, not recreated. The VPS
# still needs an R2 API token and the same bucket name; see deploy/hostinger/.env.example.
# Default: no bucket, uploads stay on the VPS volume.
# PAPERCLIP_R2_ASSETS=true
# PAPERCLIP_R2_BUCKET=paperclip
